  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1249 AM MST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\nSunday will be a chilly late Fall day with highs in the upper 40s/ \nlow 50s and light winds. Quasi-zonal flow will develop over the \nsouthwestern US, but there is a low chance another quick-hitting \nstorm impacts the area Monday/Monday night. Temperatures will \ncontinue to hover right around seasonal normals Tuesday into \nWednesday, then another quick-hitting storm looks to arrive \nThursday/Friday. Given the progressive nature of this pattern, \nsignificant precipitation looks unlikely as the residence time of a \nstorm over central and northern NM would be very short. Temperatures \nwill generally be near seasonal normals throughout the week, \nalthough the could drop below average behind one of the Pacific \nfronts if they trend stronger.",
